terictal EEG does NOT rule out epilepsy\n\n**Engel Classification** (Used for Surgical Outcomes, not initial classification):\n- **Class I**: Seizure-free (or auras only)\n- **Class II**: Rare disabling seizures\n- **Class III**: Worthwhile improvement (>75% reduction)\n- **Class IV**: No worthwhile improvement\n- This classification is primarily used to report outcomes after epilepsy surgery, not for initial diagnosis. For PTE that becomes medically refractory, the Engel classification guides assessment of surgical candidacy and outcomes.\n\n**ILAE Seizure Classification** (more relevant here):\n- This seizure is classified as: **Focal onset, with impaired awareness, evolving to bilateral tonic-clonic**\n- The focal onset (staring, behavioral arrest) followed by bilateral spread is consistent with a structural epilepsy due to known cortical lesions',
