ed to adjust your medication. Hiding seizures does not make them go away — it just means we cannot treat them properly. Can we work together on this?\'\n\n**Key Ethical Principles**:\n- **Duty to document**: The seizure must be documented in the medical record. Concealing medical events compromises care and creates legal liability.\n- **HIPAA protections**: Reassure the patient that her diagnosis is confidential and will not be shared with her employer without consent.\n- **ADA protections**: Educate her that employment discrimination based on epilepsy is illegal.\n- **Mandatory reporting**: In most states, a physician is not required to report seizures to an employer. If the state mandates DMV reporting, that obligation must be fulfilled but is separate from employer notification.\n- **Therapeutic alliance**: Validate her fear, provide concrete reassurance, and partner with her rather than dictating.',
